scratch/

# `artifacts/` is runtime output and stays ignored — with ONE deliberate hole in
# it, decided in SET_twin_tau_0p65_and_geometry_gate. A tentative gallery's two
# text files are tracked, because the site's figures name wallpapers by the IDs in
# them and a clone that cannot resolve those IDs cannot rebuild the site. The
# PICTURES stay ignored: only `gallery.jsonl` and `manifest.json` come through,
# and the un-ignore names them one by one rather than by pattern so that a third
# file appearing in a stamp is ignored until somebody decides otherwise. Git will
# not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, which is why each level is excluded by
# its contents (`dir/*`) and then re-included.
#
# **`index.html` is NOT one of them**, Matt's ruling of 2026-09-05: a record is
# its rows and its manifest, and the page is a browse view derived from them.
# `fractal-wallpapers curate solve browse <stamp>` regenerates it from
# `gallery.jsonl` on any clone, so tracking it was committing a derivation — and
# an expensive one, 4.07 MB over the seven published stamps against their rows'
# 3.60 MB. It was tracked until then and left tracking by this ruling; the files
# stay on disk.
#
# **The hole is per-stamp and the default is IGNORED**, Matt's ruling of
# 2026-09-04. It used to be per-file across every stamp, so recording a gallery
# and committing it were one act and a record too large to track was a record
# that could not be made without breaking the build. Now a record is PUBLISHED
# only when Matt names it, which is one negation line below; every other record is
# read by naming its stamp, with no durability guarantee, and is DISCARDED once
# whatever it was made to measure has been measured — Matt's ruling of 2026-09-13,
# and `CLAUDE.md` carries it as a rule a leg has to follow.
# `curation.tentative.PUBLISHED` is the same list in code and
# `tests/test_tentative.py` holds the two to agreeing.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/curation/
artifacts/curation/*
!artifacts/curation/tentative/
artifacts/curation/tentative/*
# The published stamps. Adding one is Matt's decision, not a fix.
# **Since 2026-09-29 they are the twenty-one records of 2026-09-22** — the twenty
# `final139_*` and `final140_general2000` — published together when Matt ruled
# the saved set truly finalized (`finalize_records_ckpt156`). One pattern and not
# a line each: a stamp is the UTC second its record was taken, so no record made
# after that day can match it, and on the day it was written the store held the
# keep list and nothing else. A later publication is a line of its own.
!artifacts/curation/tentative/20260922T*/
# Inside a published stamp, only the text files named here. An unpublished stamp
# is an excluded directory git never descends into, so these never reach one.
# `recipes.jsonl` says what each seat is made of — the key is a one-way digest and
# without it a clone can name a seat and not draw it.
artifacts/curation/tentative/*/*
!artifacts/curation/tentative/*/gallery.jsonl
!artifacts/curation/tentative/*/manifest.json
!artifacts/curation/tentative/*/recipes.jsonl
# Every published record is tracked whole, the n=2000's included since the
# per-file cap went to 2 MiB on 2026-09-29: no path inside a published stamp is
# ignored again, and `tests/test_tentative.py` holds that.
/labels/
/local.toml
# Every head's weights, fetched rather than tracked: `fetch-weights` reads
# `models/weights.json` for a release tag, an asset and a sha256, downloads into
# `models/<head>/`, and verifies the hash before keeping the file. The tracked
# metadata beside them — configs, metrics, scores, bars, bands — stays.
#
# ⚠ **This line is not what made `gallery_grade` unobtainable**, which is worth
# writing down because it reads like it was. Until 2026-09-14 that head had no
# `weights.json` row and no release, so nothing could fetch it at any price; the
# ignore is the same rule that hides `location.fp16.pt`, which every clone gets.
# A fetched artifact belongs out of history and un-ignoring one would put a
# fifteen-megabyte binary in a repository whose whole history is text.
models/**/*.pt
target/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
# `uv sync` is the documented install path and it writes this into the checkout,
# so a fresh clone grows a lockfile in a repository whose `README.md` says none
# is tracked — see its *Install*. One line makes that claim enforce itself
# instead of resting on the reader noticing the prose. Toolchain noise, beside
# the rest of it: the `artifacts/` hole above is per-stamp and is untouched.
/uv.lock
